## Claim under pressure
SPRINT **2.9** (MED): println walker → full `c_secret_emit_guard`.
Wave-2 security gate is **Z2**. Other gates are belt (must stay green
or be named).

| # | Gate | Expectation |
|---|------|-------------|
| Z1 | Path-A bare SECRET IDENT at `println` / `eprintln` refuse | Dual-path `ERR\tsecret` + rc≠0 (check + emit-c + emit-llvm) |
| Z2 | **Every** product println shape fail-closed | Multi-arg, concat, sink-alias, **later-arg after inner RPAREN**, same-arg after inner RPAREN, expr-pos |
| Z3 | No FP on string / comment spelling of a SECRET name | `println("tok")` ALLOW; no `ERR secret` |
| Z4 | Do not reopen 2.8 | No expand-hole relitigation |
| Z5 | emit-c compile rail: SECRET IDENT never becomes an `oo_print_*` operand | Stmt belt or front-door refuse **before** print of that IDENT |

Adversarial stance (same as wave-1): treat the check-path walker as a
**desync weapon** until every SECRET IDENT in a `println`/`eprintln`
argument list is refused on **check and every product emit**. Treat
“LLVM/wasm only print the first arg” as **accidental drop**, not a
refuse. A check `OK` on `println((n), tok)` with `// SECRET: tok` is
**FN**. An emit-c `oo_print_str(... tok ...)` is a **byte leak**.

WT `c_emit_secret.oo` (mtime 12:28, md5 `e8d9ff2d…`, 219 L) added
`depth` to the println walk **and** `c_secret_scan_call`. HEAD and
the **07:49 ELF have zero depth**. Security path-A is the shipping
host. Source-only is **untested \(U\)** until rebuilt and re-proved.

